00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.280
Slide 20, please.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:50.300
With this, we are reaffirming our full year 2026 guidance. We continue to expect net sales to grow

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.340
low single-digit and core operating income to decline low single-digit for the full year.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:01.200
For the full year 2026, we also continue to expect core net financial results to be around

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:08.960
$1.7 billion and core tax rate to be around 16.5%, both in line with our guidance from

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.420
beginning of the year. Moving to slide 21.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:21.900
As I shared previously, H1 net sales declined 2% with a strong momentum of growth drivers delivering

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:26.760
performance at the upper end of sales guidance from the start of the year. Turning to H2,

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.260
we continue to expect net sales to grow mid-single-digit as we move beyond the impact

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:40.440
of U.S. generic erosion. However, it's worth pointing out that there will be a notable difference

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.980
in the sales growth rates between the two.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:52.000
This is because we still have about $800 million of U.S. interest in the sales in previous

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.800
year Q3 base.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:02.780
We expect H2 core operating income to grow mid-to-high single-digit with continued investment

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:07.860
in our growth drivers as well as our R&D pipeline.

